{
  "0": "Add a deterministic causal repetition feature: multiply each existing item input embedding by 1 + 0.25*log1p(c), where c counts that item's earlier occurrences in the available training prefix. Compute before padding, using no future events; reproduce at inference. This may help the GRU distinguish repeated preferences from exploratory interactions. Keep embedding parameters, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer unchanged across all four categories.",
  "1": "Use two stacked GRU layers of the baseline hidden width, with a residual connection adding the first layer's output to the second layer's output before the existing readout. This may let the second recurrent layer refine longer dependencies while retaining first-layer signals and improving gradient flow. Preserve input features, embeddings, scoring, history selection, readout, loss and optimizer; train one network per category.",
  "2": "Cap each causal input history at its 20 most recent interactions, preserving chronological order and using the identical truncation during training and prediction. Shorter context may reduce interference from stale interests and improve next-item ranking in sparse Amazon histories. Preserve target examples, supplied splits, feature definitions, embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer across all four categories.",
  "3": "Keep the baseline optimizer and initial learning rate, but apply cosine learning-rate decay to 10% of that rate over the configured training epochs, capped at 200. This may preserve early learning speed while allowing finer updates late in training. Keep batch size, dropout, weight decay, model, features, readout and loss unchanged; retain training seed 42 and one selected checkpoint per category."
